Lineage
-------
1. Antigravity on Android — pioneered by werdio325-png
   (github.com/werdio325-png/antigravity-android): running Google's
   Antigravity engine natively in an Android userspace sandbox.
2. Leostryx — by Leostrange (github.com/Leostrange/Leostryx): custom
   model providers, MCP integration, developer toolchain and security
   governance built on that foundation.
3. Hibou — this repository's earlier releases, maintained by ovrrup:
   heavily based on the projects above. A rebrand with an English-first
   interface; only the identity changed and bugs were fixed — no
   substantial engine changes.
4. Kestrel — the current product: a complete rebuild. The engine is
   reimplemented 1:1 in native Kotlin, the user interface is redesigned
   from scratch (terminal-mono-graphite console), and identity, icons
   and the build pipeline are new.

